# Finish summary (Agents panel)

When you **finish work** as an agent launched from the Agents panel
(`.cursor/agents`), **always print one JSON line with a `title` field** at the
very end — a short summary of what you did (e.g. “Updated README and rules”,
“Code review – 3 files”). The Cretli frontend parses this and updates the
displayed run name.

**Format (one line, at the end of the output):**
```json
{"title": "Short summary of what was done (max ~50 characters)"}
```

**Rules:**
- Only **one** JSON line, **at the end** of your output (after every other
  message, before you stop).
- `title` is a string — a short name/summary (no raw quotes inside, or escape
  `\"`).
- No other text on that same line — the frontend looks for exactly this JSON.
- If you omit it, the run name stays the default (the agent file name).

**Example ending:**
```
... (your normal output) ...
{"title": "Updated documentation in .cursor/rules"}
```
